===Verb===
{{en-verb|rethinks|rethinking|rethought}}

# To [[think]] again about something, with the intention of changing or replacing it.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=08 Dec 91|volume=19|number=21|journal=Gay Community News|page=8|author=Liz Galst|title=Gay Male Incest Survivors,  Safer Sex, and AIDS|text=There's a myth that incest survivors are an extremely small percentage of the gay male community. But that belief is something that needs to be '''rethought'''. One in six men (gay and straight) polled in a 1985 ''Los Angeles Times'' survey reported being sexually abused before the age of 18.}}
#: {{ux|en|Disability rights advocates are encouraging people to '''rethink''' the words "crazy" and "insane" as they stigmatize mental health.}}

